      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "hmm yes have VRChat cracking down on copyrighted material (avatars) when they don't own the rights to said avatars.... That sounds like a legal mess.\nThe person who created these avatars are the ones holding the rights to the avatars they made, if another user uploaded this avatar as say a public avatar and is violating the terms of that specific avatar as a result, it's up to the avatar creator to take action. \nBasically the avatar creator is the one responsible for copyright violations as they hold the rights to that avatar and they can DMCA content off the platform and maybe even get the user who uploaded said avatars without permission banned. But VRChat itself can't really do much.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
